note kernel.om: every fn here becomes an OpenCL kernel in kernel.spv and is also
note compiled to a native AArch64 program. reference.py must give the expected value.
note Scalar types: uchar ushort uint ulong byte short int long bool; at most 6 parameters.

note Average of two uint values, rounded down, without overflow: a + b can need 33 bits.
fn avg a uint b uint to uint
ret add and a b shr xor a b uint 1
end

note Greatest common divisor (Euclid). Loops carry a bound; 64 rounds cover any 32-bit pair.
fn gcd a uint b uint to uint
while ne b 0 bound 64
t = rem a b
a = b
b = t
end
ret a
end

note Clamp x into lo..hi; an empty range traps with code 3 on both targets.
fn clamp x int lo int hi int to int
if gt lo hi
trap 3
end
if lt x lo
ret lo
end
if gt x hi
ret hi
end
ret x
end
